# DX - Multi-Channel Messaging Gateway
DX is a powerful multi-channel messaging gateway with AI agent support, built on the OpenClaw foundation.
## Features
- **Multi-Channel Support**: WhatsApp, Telegram, Slack, Discord, Google Chat, Signal, iMessage, and more
- **AI Agent Integration**: Built-in support for AI-powered conversations
- **Provider Support**: Works with multiple messaging providers and channels
- **Extensible**: Plugin system for custom integrations
## Quick Start
### Prerequisites
- Bun >= 1.0.0
- Node.js >= 22.12.0
### Installation
```bash
# Install dependencies
bun install
# Build the project
bun run build
# Start the gateway
bun run start
```
### Development
```bash
# Run in development mode
bun run dev
# Run the gateway with auto-reload
bun run gateway:watch
# Run tests
bun test
```
## Configuration
Configuration files are located in `~/.dx/` directory. The main configuration file is `dx.json`.
Example minimal configuration:
```json
{
  "agent": {
    "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4-5"
  },
  "channels": {
    "telegram": {
      "botToken": "YOUR_BOT_TOKEN"
    }
  }
}
```
## Available Commands
- `bun scripts/run-node.mjs gateway` - Start the gateway server
- `bun scripts/run-node.mjs chat` - Simple terminal chat interface (NEW!)
- `bun scripts/run-node.mjs tui` - Full-featured terminal UI
- `bun scripts/run-node.mjs agent` - Run agent commands
- `bun scripts/run-node.mjs channels` - Manage messaging channels
- `bun scripts/run-node.mjs status` - Check system status
- `bun run build` - Build the project
- `bun test` - Run tests
### Chat Command (Quick Start)
The new `chat` command provides a simple way to interact with your AI agent:
```bash
# Start the gateway first
bun scripts/run-node.mjs gateway
# In another terminal, start chat
bun scripts/run-node.mjs chat
# With options
bun scripts/run-node.mjs chat --session work --model google-antigravity/claude-opus-4-5-thinking
```
See [CHAT_USAGE.md](./CHAT_USAGE.md) for complete documentation.
## Channels
DX supports the following messaging channels:
- WhatsApp (via Baileys)
- Telegram
- Discord
- Slack
- Google Chat
- Signal
- iMessage
- Microsoft Teams
- Matrix
- And more...
